Article 2: The Intellectual Property Court shall hear the following appeal cases:
(1) Administrative appeal cases concerning the authorization and confirmation of patents, new plant varieties, and integrated circuit layout designs;
(2) Civil and administrative appeal cases concerning the ownership and infringement of invention patents, new plant varieties, and integrated circuit layout designs;
(3) Major and complex civil and administrative appeal cases concerning the ownership and infringement of utility model patents, technical secrets, and computer software;
(4) Civil and administrative appeal cases concerning monopolies.
The Intellectual Property Court shall hear the following other cases:
(1) Major and complex first-instance civil and administrative cases of the types specified in the preceding paragraph nationwide;
(2) Cases in which the trial supervision procedure is applied according to law, such as applications for retrial, protests, and retrials, with respect to the legally effective judgments, rulings, and mediation agreements of the first-instance civil and administrative cases specified in the preceding paragraph;
(3) Cases concerning jurisdictional disputes over the first-instance civil and administrative cases specified in the preceding paragraph, applications for reconsideration of rulings on conduct preservation, applications for reconsideration of decisions on fines and detention, and requests for extension of the trial period;
(4) Other cases that the Supreme People's Court considers should be heard by the Intellectual Property Court.
